{"name":"Bush","hex":"#0d2e1c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Middle English.\n\nGeorge H. W. Bush, 41st president of the United States from 1989 to 1993","George H. W. Bush, 41st president of the United States from 1989 to 1993"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bush (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"The surname Bush is derived from either the Old English word \"busc\" or the Old Norse \"buskr,\" both of which mean \"bush,\" a shrub, and was probably used for someone who lived in a bushy area."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bush_(surname)","wikidata":"Q1484464"},{"title":"Bush family","blocks":[{"text":"The Bush family is an American political family that has played a prominent role in American politics since the 1950s, foremost as the first family of the United States from 1989 to 1993, during the presidency of George H. W. Bush, and again from 2001 to 2009, during the presidency of George W. Bush. They also played prominent roles in areas of American news, sports, entertainment, and business. They were also the second family of the United States from 1981 to 1989, during the vice presidency of George H. W. Bush. The Bush family is one of four families to have produced two presidents of the United States by the same surname; the others were the Adams, Roosevelt, and Harrison families."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bush_family","wikidata":"Q2743830"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/SP_BUSH_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-SP_BUSH_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/SP_BUSH_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-SP_BUSH_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/